1. Install Apache web server and PHP on your Linux machine, then create an index.php file that displays 'Welcome to My Foodie Blog' when accessed via your browser.
=>apt-get install -y apache2 php libapache2-mod-php
Created /var/www/html/index.php:
PHP<?php echo "Welcome to My Foodie Blog"; ?>
Verified:
Bashcurl http://localhost/index.php
Output: Welcome to My Foodie Blog

2. Configure your Apache server to serve a custom 404 error page that displays a Zomato-style message: 'Oops! This page is as empty as your cart.'
=>Created /var/www/html/404.html:
HTML<h1>Oops! This page is as empty as your cart.</h1>
Configured in Apache (ErrorDocument 404 /404.html).
Test:
Bashcurl http://localhost/nonexistent
Returns the custom message with HTTP 404.

