5. Edit your Apache configuration to restrict access to a specific directory (e.g., /var/www/html/secret) so that only users from localhost (127.0.0.1) can access it.<br><br><em><strong>Hint:</strong> Use the 'Require' directive in your Apache config or .htaccess file.</em>
=>mkdir -p /var/www/html/secret
echo "Secret content - only localhost" > /var/www/html/secret/index.html
Restricted with .htaccess:
textRequire local
Enabled AllowOverride All and reloaded Apache.
Result: Access from localhost succeeds (HTTP 200). The Require local directive limits access to 127.0.0.1 / ::1 only.
